{"title":"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_polygon\" title=\"Convex polygon\">convex</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hexagon\" title=\"Hexagon\">hexagon</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, all six sides are congruent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae15cd6fc137587ad1676133c8342dc210dc6364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">right angles</a>, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4280048f14039e799902b03ebe3447a09d680ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B, \\angle C, \\angle E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49cad7f8bf72cf2d150b5dc9eeecdc38bf919f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle F$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent\">congruent</a>. The area of the hexagonal region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd930caa4f2afe0e623387e0e234753408a657c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2116(\\sqrt{2}+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side length be called <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b955bec140be2d953a0054026660efb822729e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=AB=BC=CD=DE=EF=AF$\" width=\"329\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2006_II_AIME-1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/89/2006_II_AIME-1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f087142d8c53e1237d2c086e4e5c1b39718f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=\\sqrt{AB^2+AF^2}=\\sqrt{x^2+x^2}=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"318\" height=\"19\" />. Then the areas of the triangles AFB and CDE in total are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab270f3b7a8cc001830766dbcd4da3c0c45680a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{2}\\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"41\" />,\nand the area of the rectangle BCEF equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38febda2ed76dcd98b96e00a7928e27070c48824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\cdot x\\sqrt{2}=x^2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Then we have to solve the equation \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a496e165fdff684d02fb58c1cf7ad5243a7de77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2116(\\sqrt{2}+1)=x^2\\sqrt{2}+x^2\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b83ddfe173279527aaffeb6523d3bc42e07dc50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2116(\\sqrt{2}+1)=x^2(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f24b4c5143d4d094127e21d683b8392a25fc235.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2116=x^2\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c54704eca22496b7a8e78db66bccbad5be1d25.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=46\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba506a21078ffb7216d69962fbd85ceb0542934f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{046}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d1bdfa75074455b09acbe4d1a5007d9f1674e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4056d41f42aa8a00adca0ff5d1209b6bb0e92d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef820980d93fb66d6f4b2883b9630d6bbdfd2667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle E$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49cad7f8bf72cf2d150b5dc9eeecdc38bf919f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle F$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> are congruent, the degree-measure of each of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434af9e041436ef3a84987dc42387b7c8fa88072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${{720-2\\cdot90}\\over4}= 135$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" />. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> divide the hexagonal region into two right triangles and a rectangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598141cec89bb44405e53c44ba75a25f8b5981bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dfc9e27bb3976d610c3f53fcbde6c44f2be7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=x\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4eac99a9d419ae9b76ff89eae925b572923827.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2116(\\sqrt2+1)&amp;=[ABCDEF]\\\\ &amp;=2\\cdot {1\\over2}x^2+x\\cdot x\\sqrt2=x^2(1+\\sqrt2), \\end{align*}\" width=\"379\" height=\"66\" />so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0ac186742196b9df331524b8839c96d38b261b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=2116$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80933e53b3ab31d15e1297d8d1cd0d3d10fb4b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{046}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"75\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6f562c7200788c6151d82e78f798fb3a90000d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F; A=(0,0); B=(7,0); C=(13,6); E=(6,13); D=(13,13); F=(0,7); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(E); dot(F); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle,linewidth(0.7)); label(&quot;{\\tiny $A$}&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;{\\tiny $B$}&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;{\\tiny $C$}&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;{\\tiny $D$}&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;{\\tiny $E$}&quot;,E,N); label(&quot;{\\tiny $F$}&quot;,F,W); [/asy]\" width=\"245\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> to intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> to intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are 135 degrees, so minor angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> apart of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> respectively are 45 degrees. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e45b103025e03dff2afa47edc6e02c2f4ba23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GB = GC = HE = HF = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"228\" height=\"14\" />, so we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c3e7af93e33a79fed6c6b590a6376641b999de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC = \\dots = FA = a\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"239\" height=\"21\" />. The two side lengths of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/977dfcb93d778235d5a81f79eebea6af55ec83ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGDH$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are equal and the measure in degrees of all figures are 90, so the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/977dfcb93d778235d5a81f79eebea6af55ec83ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGDH$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a square. It follows that the side length of this square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f869b1bacd3527fd45e24b226e7bc883b291fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + a\\sqrt{2} = a(\\sqrt{2}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"24\" />, and the area of this figure is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89cef89a9a351a3d74a1eabdbfb9a3313f55358a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a(\\sqrt{2}+1))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"24\" />. The area of the hexagon is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8255e0478a26f8d63a24c81b1dc563423a1d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a(\\sqrt{2}+1))^2 - a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"24\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b3bd9397e5ab1bd11da78fb49da9220259087b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2((\\sqrt{2}+1)^2 - 1) = 2116(\\sqrt{2}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"272\" height=\"24\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875afa7a59d5fd536d91bcb9efc069dc957f294e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2(\\sqrt{2}+1) = 2116(\\sqrt{2}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"24\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f372db1f6439bc56382bdeea097c8afabb2ab41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}a = 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41bbb5ef9b72f769c542c02945e22e93bd11284c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{46}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />. The side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347971a51bf91ecee0bf15b003f0c189d709bf2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d381ff29c1c60b769aa27e3598f3fe0ebdba62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{46}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} = \\boxed{046}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II\" title=\"2006 AIME II\">2006 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wik